description     "NVIDIA bluetooth/wifi init script"
#
# L4T on Xiaomi Mi Pad 1 (mocha / Tegra K1) - Bluetooth bring-up
#
# WORKING CONFIGURATION (verified at boot on 2026-10-25 16:04 and 16:22).
#
# 1) DO NOT re-add low-power mode.  The stock file had:
#        echo 1 > /proc/bluetooth/sleep/lpm
#        brcm_patchram_plus ... --enable_lpm --tosleep=50000 ...
#    The LPM wake path does not work on this board: the BCM43341 sleeps and
#    never answers another HCI command (even HCI Reset 0x0c03 times out).
#
# 2) DO NOT add --patchram: /lib/firmware/BCM4350C0.hcd targets a different
#    chip and brcm_patchram_plus hangs on it forever.  It is not needed.
#
# 3) rfkill lives at /usr/sbin/rfkill on 14.04 (NOT /sbin/rfkill).
#
# 4) This job is started by /etc/udev/rules.d/99-nv-wifibt.rules when the
#    bluedroid_pm rfkill state changes.  Do not add extra rfkill calls here:
#    flipping the state makes that same rule fire `initctl stop ...` and kill
#    this job.
#
# 5) post-start writes a valid BD_ADDR (fixed, see bt-mac-setup.sh): the
#    controller otherwise reports the placeholder 43:50:C0:00:00:00 and other
#    devices ignore its inquiry responses.
#
instance $SUBTASK

script
	exec /usr/sbin/rfkill unblock bluetooth
	exec /usr/sbin/brcm_patchram_plus --enable_hci --scopcm=0,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0 --baudrate 115200 --no2bytes /dev/ttyTHS2
end script

post-start script
	/usr/local/sbin/bt-mac-setup.sh
end script
